------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Acknowledgements (design patterns studied; no code copied)
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The following HackApertus 2026 projects documented patterns or findings that
shaped this protocol. No code from them is included; they are credited for their
ideas and reports.

  AlpenRecht (github.com/Anakalypto/AlpenRecht, Apache-2.0): choose labels,
    not list positions; keyword top-up only when the model failed.
  apertus-qa (github.com/ventolabs-hq/apertus-qa, Apache-2.0): JSON generation
    with a rule-based fallback and an explicit "refuse" action.
  b2bern (github.com/Spaghetti-Overflow/hack-apertus-stregoni, Apache-2.0):
    argument validation against a JSON schema, a name allow-list, a cap on
    tool calls, de-duplicated ids, one repair turn that does not echo values.
  Bern-Fit (github.com/Grozby/kinder-bueno, MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 Grozby):
    a bounded native tool loop with recovery of calls written as text.
  Connect-Bern (github.com/CPD9/bern-life, Apache-2.0, Copyright 2026 Peter
    Dike and contributors): a JSON step protocol with one repair round.
  gemeindesim (github.com/hatif03/gemeindesim, Apache-2.0): placeholder
    examples instead of filled examples in the format prompt; dropping an
    unclosed reasoning span (strip_reasoning_spans), rewritten in parse.py;
    the report of a strict-mode whitespace runaway on another gateway.
  mutz (github.com/beSaif/mutz, MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 beSaif and Jumainah
    Khan): the report that -thinking variants refuse tool_choice.
  rosetta-flow (github.com/anesask/rosetta-flow, Apache-2.0): nonce-fenced
    data markers (the idea behind delimit()), and the report of template tokens
    leaking into text.
  apertus-fracture (RishiksaiP/BEA-16B; code Apache-2.0, report CC-BY-4.0 per
    its listing; repository not read): reports of native tool-parser issues on
    Apertus (tool_call_id dropped by the template, parallel results mixed up).
  guptachetan1995/apertus (Apache-2.0, Copyright (c) 2026 Chetan Gupta): a
    single invoke chokepoint; write actions are never registered.
  Berkeley Function Calling Leaderboard (BFCL): the benchmark categories and
    AST-style scoring, through ArchAI's tool_bench.
